-\section{Comparability Audit Across All 58 Core Families}\label{sec:defenses}
-\subsection{Unified 58-core disposition and 39-record ledger}
-Across all \FinalCore{} core families in our unified collection (43 from the October 8 snapshot plus 15 from the October 21 expansion), every family has a verified intervention disposition (Supplement S5 (Table~S11)): \textbf{20 families evaluate mitigation components} (16 snapshot + 4 additions: \texttt{wu2026cacheprune}, \texttt{lee2026otro}, \texttt{chen2026sparleak}, \texttt{hadad2026shape}), two use fixed guardrails, five evaluate interventions for other objectives or split-decoy boundaries (4 snapshot + \texttt{politis2026splitdecoy}), 22 report no mitigation evaluation within the inspected scope (13 snapshot + 9 additions), five are Type~IV authorized diagnostic components (4 snapshot + \texttt{revankar2026mirage}), and four contain unbound quantitative defense assertions. The 20 evaluated-mitigation families and contextual comparators contribute \textbf{39 source-bound result records} (33 in the baseline snapshot plus 6 from the four October~21 mitigation additions) and \textbf{78 utility/cost field positions}. Table~\ref{tab:defense-types} organizes the eight intervention families by threat polarity (Types~I--III), receiving view and deployment boundary.
-\input{tables/defense-types}
-
-\subsection{Within-family and within-cohort record comparisons}
-While the machine-readable audit retains all $\binom{33}{2}=528$ baseline pairs for completeness, 426 pairs cross unrelated mechanism cohorts and are outside scope by construction. The 13 within-family pairs are included in the 102 within-cohort pairs: $528=426+102$, with no additional subtraction of 13. Focusing on the \textbf{13 within-family pairs} (multiple records inside the same paper) and \textbf{102 within-cohort related pairs} (66 traffic-envelope, 28 cache-service, 3 behavioral-humanization, 3 generator-fingerprint, 1 local-memory, 1 fixed-instruction; Supplement S8) reveals why paper-level comparisons fail:
-\begin{itemize}
