 \subsection{What the cases establish}
 The experiments connect concrete failure modes to the audit's comparison obligations. E5 isolates emitter-dependent cost and count leakage. E6/E7 show that adaptive fitting and encrypted size decoding expose residual tool-intent signals. E9 extends the evidence to real agents and training-only defense calibration: prompt compliance can coexist with high leakage, while online shaping substantially reduces the measured signal at a quantified cost. Together, the cases turn the audit into an executable evaluation sequence: bind the emitted trace, isolate cover effects, fit attackers on defended data, and price protection on the held-out workload.
